let me briefly show you  a high-level overview about our  journey in the last couple of months  we called our development program for a  covet 19  vaccine project light speed because you  can't go  faster than light and this was what we  aimed for this journey started in  january this year and was devoted  to the development of a well-tolerated  and effective covit-19 vaccine  following the highest scientific and  ethical standards  this was a journey of 11 10 to 11 months  which started with engineering multiple  potential candidates vaccine candidates  of which several entered clinical  testing  phase one in april this year in july  we selected together with our partner  pfizer  one of those candidates the most  promising one for a large phase free  trial  and in november this year we could  report  that in this trial our vaccine has met  all primary efficacy endpoints  on the next slide you can see that  project lightspeed is in fact  a global concerted larger scale effort  our phase free trial has been conducted  in multiple countries in the u.s  argentina brazil germany south africa  and in turkey the phase 3  trial has reached the final end points  in mid november in addition to  that we have regular regulatory  submissions  on a rolling basis ongoing not only  in the eu but also additional countries  such as canada  and australia we have in addition  an application at the usfda  for emergency use authorization  of our vaccine in in the u.s  and we are awaiting decisions by the  fda mid of december  and this is also the time horizon in  which we  expect decisions of the ema  on our conditional marketing  authorization  application
 

